course: dictionary
lesson: 16170
title: Wriggly and what it describes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wriggly means twisting and turning a lot. A worm is wriggly because it moves its whole body in wavy bends. «The wriggly worm slid back into the soil.» The clue is the word worm, which tells you what is moving and how.
explain: Wriggly can also describe a person, especially a child, who cannot keep still. «The wriggly toddler kept climbing off her chair.» The clue is that she keeps moving when she should be sitting still. Check your meaning by swapping in "could not keep still": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Wriggly is used for lines too. «Draw a wriggly line across the page.» A wriggly line is wavy, with lots of little bends, not straight. When you meet wriggly, ask: what is moving or bending here? The answer tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Wriggly is an adjective, and its forms are wrigglier and wriggliest.
fact: «Wriggly» means twisting and turning a lot, like a worm or a fish.
fact: «Wriggly» can describe a child who cannot keep still.
fact: A «wriggly line» is wavy, with lots of little bends.
exercise: «The wriggly worm was looking for food.» What does wriggly describe in this sentence? | A bowl of cold soup | A tall, straight tree | *A worm twisting its body | A sleeping cat
exercise: «Ben was too wriggly to sit through the film.» What does wriggly mean here? | Covered in mud | Ready to sleep | Very quiet and calm | *Could not keep still
exercise: Mia drew a «wriggly line» on her page. What does a wriggly line look like? | Broken into dots | *Wavy, with lots of little bends | Straight and flat | Thick and black
test: «The fish gave a wriggly flick of its tail.» What does wriggly mean here? | Happy and loud | Very cold | *Twisting and turning | Sleepy and slow
test: Mrs Patel said, «Sit still, you are so wriggly today!» What does wriggly describe? | A puddle of rain | A wavy line on paper | *A child who cannot keep still | A worm in the garden
exam: Which sentence uses wriggly to describe a child who cannot keep still? | «The wriggly fish swam around the pond.» | «The wriggly line curled across the page.» | «The wriggly worm wiggled under the leaves.» | *«The wriggly toddler could not stay in his seat.»
